given-names></name><name><surname>Stanton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Transcriptome profiling of human and murine ESCs identifies divergent paths required to maintain the stem cell state</article-title><source>Stem Cells</source><year>2005</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>166</fpage><lpage>185</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15671141</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1634/stemcells.2004-0162</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Addicks</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Glennon</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Zwaka</surname><given-names>TP</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>BMP4 initiates human embryonic stem cell differentiation to trophoblast</article-title><source>Nat Biotechnol</source><year>2002</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1261</fpage><lpage>1264</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12426580</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nbt761</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rosler</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Fisk</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ares</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Irving</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Miura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><g